# ─── .NET build output (regenerated by `dotnet restore` / `dotnet build`) ───
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/

# ─── Visual Studio / Rider IDE cache and user-specific files ───
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs
*.csproj.Backup.tmp

# ─── Test / coverage results ───
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
*.coverage
*.coveragexml
coverage/

# ─── Local run logs ───
*.log

# ─── Claude Code local settings (machine-specific permissions) ───
.claude/settings.local.json

# ─── OS junk ───
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: the following are intentionally NOT ignored — the project needs them
# to build and run after a fresh clone:
#   certs/devcert.pfx   → referenced by appsettings.json (Kestrel HTTPS)
#   appsettings*.json   → app configuration (no real secrets)
#   Properties/launchSettings.json → defines the 5269 / 7267 ports
#
# If you prefer NOT to commit the dev certificate, uncomment the line below and
# regenerate it locally with:
#   dotnet dev-certs https -ep certs/devcert.pfx -p devcert
# certs/*.pfx
